  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Lord said … Who hath made man’s mouth, Ex. 4:11. I will be with thy mouth, and teach thee, Ex. 4:12. With him will I speak mouth to mouth, Num. 12:8. lay upon the child, and put his mouth upon his mouth, 2 Kgs. 4:34. Out of the mouth of babes, Ps. 8:2 (Matt. 21:16). I will keep my mouth with a bridle, Ps. 39:1. mouth of them that speak lies shall be stopped, Ps. 63:11. They have mouths, but they speak not, Ps. 115:5. Set a watch, O Lord, before my mouth, Ps. 141:3. mouth of the foolish is near destruction, Prov. 10:14. mouth of the just bringeth forth wisdom, Prov. 10:31. satisfied with good by the fruit of his mouth, Prov. 12:14. He that keepeth his mouth keepeth his life, Prov. 13:3. A fool’s mouth is his destruction, Prov. 18:7. Whoso keepeth his mouth and his tongue keepeth his soul, Prov. 21:23. people draw near me with their mouth, Isa. 29:13 (Matt. 15:8; 2 Ne. 27:25). afflicted, yet he opened not his mouth, Isa. 53:7 (Mosiah 14:7). I will make my words in thy mouth fire, Jer. 5:14. I will open thy mouth, and thou shalt say unto them, Ezek. 3:27. with their mouth they shew much love, Ezek. 33:31. a mouth speaking great things, Dan. 7:8 (Rev. 13:5). law of truth was in his mouth, Mal. 2:6.",
